          "question": "Why is osteoarthritis not simply “wear and tear” of a joint?",
          "answer": "Osteoarthritis (OA) is often misunderstood as merely \"wear and tear.\" However, it is a complex condition that involves several factors, not just mechanical stress. While aging and joint injury can contribute to OA, the disease also involves changes in the joint's cartilage, bone, and surrounding tissues.\n\nThe idea of \"wear and tear\" oversimplifies the process. OA is characterized by a combination of biomechanical, genetic, inflammatory, and metabolic factors that affect joint health. For instance, inflammation plays a significant role in the progression of the disease. It is also influenced by lifestyle factors and coexisting health conditions.\n\nI cannot cover detailed biological mechanisms or specific treatment approaches for OA in this response. If you have more specific aspects of osteoarthritis in mind, feel free to ask!\n\nNot medical advice. This is an educational software project. It does not diagnose or treat, and it must not be used for real medical decisions.",
